  data: {
    LLM: 'Count card points carefully and protect high trumps. Do not declare going out unless you can verify at least 66 points.\n\nUse marriages to accelerate scoring, but time declarations so the announced cards are not immediately lost. Consider closing the talon when you have the lead, trump control, and enough winners to reach 66 under strict follow-suit play.\n\nTrack all high cards and estimate the opponent’s remaining point ceiling. Closing the talon is powerful only when your hand can force the last tricks; a failed close gives the opponent a large score.',
